a file coordinator without a daemon must still run the accessor

submitIntent turned any XPC error into an NSError, and coordinateReadingItemAtURL treats an error as
a reason NOT to call the reader. filecoordinationd is a LaunchDaemon, so without launchd there is no
daemon at all, and every coordinated read in the process silently did nothing.

That is what stopped iA Writer indexing. Its library rows all read Updating forever, which the
application chooses when the excerpt string is empty, and the excerpt was empty because the body
column of its own index was NULL for every file. FC_DEBUG=1 named it once per document:

    FC:355: submitting intent for path /Users/root/Documents/IndexProbe.md with options 5
    FC:394: daemon replied to intent message with message: <OS_xpc_error: Connection invalid>
    FC:397: daemon indicated failure/denial to perform operation
    FC:425: invoking user block synchronously with error

Coordination is ADVISORY. A daemon that cannot be reached means nobody is coordinating, so the
accessor must still run: refusing the read loses the access entirely, which is far worse than taking
it uncoordinated. A daemon that answers and DENIES is a different thing and still errors as before.

The completion handshake is skipped in that case because there is no reply object to build it from,
and because the wait it arms would never be signalled.

